# Every float literal of the test folds to its bits (float-lits), also those
# whose flag simp replaced by a discriminant or a join point's parameter: no
# call of Float.ofScientific or Float32.ofScientific is left in the loop,
# so lean2rr's allocations do not grow with N (FACTOR 0). A call left there
# takes the slow path (exponent above 22, or above 10 for Float32) at each
# iteration, and that path allocates big numbers. Native Lean calls them at
# each iteration (its allocations grow; FACTOR 0 ignores them).
1000 | 4000 | 0 200
